hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"234","Ṭāfa an-Nabiyyu ṣallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam bil-bayti ʿalā baʿīrin, kullamā atā ar-rakna ashāra ilayhi bi-shayʿin ʿindahu wa kabbara.. The Prophet (peace be upon him) performed Tawaf around the House (the Kaaba) on a camel. Whenever he came to the Corner (the Black Stone), he pointed at it with something he had with him and said \Allahu Akbar\"" (Takbir)."""
"235","Rabbana atina fi al-dunya hasanatan wa fi al-akhirati hasanatan wa qina 'adhab al-nar. \Our Lord"," give us in this world [that which is] good and in the Hereafter [that which is] good and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.\"""""
